      "id": "maxima-minima",
      "title": "Maxima & Minima",
      "subtopics": [
        "Critical/stationary points",
        "First-derivative test",
        "Second-derivative test, inflection points",
        "Local vs global extrema",
        "Absolute extrema on closed intervals (endpoints!)",
        "Convexity (f''>0) and uniqueness of minimum"
      ],
      "estHours": 5,
      "priority": "high",
      "tips": "On [a,b], always evaluate endpoints too. f''>0 everywhere means at most one critical point (a global min) but a minimum need not exist (e.g. e^x). Second-derivative test is inconclusive when f''=0.",
